IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cla-nouns`

-- Civil Law Act 1909 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 15/10/2024)
-- LAYER 1 -- section 4: insolvent estates and winding up, waste, merger, mortgagors, assignment of debts,
-- stipulations, injunctions and receivers, interim relief in aid of foreign proceedings, equity to prevail.
--
-- Each subsection is one function (a regulative rule as well for s 4(3)).  The open-textured antecedents are plain
-- yes/no inputs; the pre-23 July 1909 and pre-1879 equity the Act points to is not re-run.
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer".

§ `Section 4(1) and (2) -- insolvent estates and winding up`

-- src:254 | 4.—(1) In the administration by any court of the assets of any
-- src:255 | deceased person whose estate proves to be insufficient for the
-- src:256 | payment in full of his debts and liabilities, and in the winding up of
-- src:257 | any company under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution
-- src:258 | Act 2018 whose assets prove to be insufficient for the payment of its
-- src:259 | debts and liabilities and the costs of winding up, the same rules shall
-- src:260 | prevail and be observed as to the respective rights of secured and
-- src:261 | unsecured creditors, and as to debts and liabilities provable, and as to
-- src:262 | the valuation of annuities and future and contingent liabilities
-- src:263 | respectively, as are in force for the time being under the law of
-- src:264 | bankruptcy with respect to the estates of persons adjudged bankrupt.
@ref s 4(1) (src:254-264)
GIVEN `the kind of administration` IS A `Kind of insolvent administration`
      `the question is about the respective rights of secured and unsecured creditors or the debts and liabilities provable or the valuation of annuities and future and contingent liabilities` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(1) the rules in force under the law of bankruptcy prevail and are to be observed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of administration` EQUALS `Another kind of administration` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the administration by any court of the assets of any deceased person whose estate proves to be insufficient ... and in the winding up of any company under the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018"
        IF `the question is about the respective rights of secured and unsecured creditors or the debts and liabilities provable or the valuation of annuities and future and contingent liabilities` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the same rules shall prevail ... as to the respective rights of secured and unsecured creditors, and as to debts and liabilities provable, and as to the valuation of annuities and future and contingent liabilities"

-- src:270 | (2) All persons who, in any such case, would be entitled to prove for
-- src:271 | and receive dividends out of the estate of any such deceased person,
-- src:272 | or out of the assets of any such company, may come in under the
-- src:273 | decree or order for the administration of such estate, or under the
-- src:278 | winding up of such company, and make such claims against the same
-- src:279 | as they may respectively be entitled to by virtue of this Act.
@ref s 4(2) (src:270-279)
GIVEN `the kind of administration` IS A `Kind of insolvent administration`
      `the person would be entitled to prove for and receive dividends out of the estate or the assets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(2) the person may come in under the decree or order and make claims against the estate or the company` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of administration` EQUALS `Another kind of administration` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any such case"
        IF `the person would be entitled to prove for and receive dividends out of the estate or the assets` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "All persons who ... would be entitled to prove for and receive dividends"

§ `Section 4(3) to (6) -- waste and merger`

-- src:283 | (3) A tenant for life or lives or a leasehold tenant shall not commit
-- src:284 | voluntary waste; but this subsection shall not apply to any estate or
-- src:285 | tenancy without impeachment of waste, or affect any licence or other
-- src:286 | right to commit waste.
@ref s 4(3) (src:283-286)
GIVEN `the kind of tenant` IS A `Kind of tenant`
      `the estate or tenancy is without impeachment of waste` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tenant has a licence or other right to commit waste` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the tenant may commit voluntary waste` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of tenant` EQUALS `Another kind of occupier` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A tenant for life or lives or a leasehold tenant shall not commit voluntary waste"
        IF `the estate or tenancy is without impeachment of waste` OR `the tenant has a licence or other right to commit waste` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "this subsection shall not apply to any estate or tenancy without impeachment of waste, or affect any licence or other right to commit waste" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not commit voluntary waste"

-- The same prohibition as a yes/no question: does the prohibition of s 4(3) apply to this tenant?
-- src:283 | (3) A tenant for life or lives or a leasehold tenant shall not commit
-- src:284 | voluntary waste; but this subsection shall not apply to any estate or
-- src:285 | tenancy without impeachment of waste, or affect any licence or other
-- src:286 | right to commit waste.
@ref s 4(3) the prohibition applies (src:283-286)
GIVEN `the kind of tenant` IS A `Kind of tenant`
      `the estate or tenancy is without impeachment of waste` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tenant has a licence or other right to commit waste` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(3) the prohibition of voluntary waste applies to the tenant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the kind of tenant` EQUALS `Another kind of occupier` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A tenant for life or lives or a leasehold tenant"
        IF `the estate or tenancy is without impeachment of waste` OR `the tenant has a licence or other right to commit waste` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this subsection shall not apply to any estate or tenancy without impeachment of waste, or affect any licence or other right to commit waste"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The prohibition as a regulative rule: the tenant SHANT commit voluntary waste (no time limit is stated).
@ref s 4(3) the prohibition as a regulative rule (src:283-286)
GIVEN `the prohibition applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under section 4(3)` `Act under section 4(3)`
`s 4(3) the tenant shall not commit voluntary waste` MEANS
    IF `the prohibition applies`
    THEN
        PARTY `The tenant for life or leasehold tenant`
        SHANT `commit voluntary waste`
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `The tenant for life or leasehold tenant` BECAUSE "voluntary waste committed contrary to s 4(3)"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:288 | (4) A tenant who infringes subsection (3) shall be liable in damages
-- src:289 | to his remainderman or reversioner; and in subsection (3), “leasehold
-- src:290 | tenant” includes a tenant for a term, a tenant under a periodical
-- src:291 | tenancy and a tenant at will.
@ref s 4(4) (src:288-291)
GIVEN `the tenant has infringed subsection (3) by committing voluntary waste when the prohibition applied to the tenant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4) the tenant is liable in damages to the remainderman or reversioner` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the tenant has infringed subsection (3) by committing voluntary waste when the prohibition applied to the tenant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A tenant who infringes subsection (3)"

-- src:289 | to his remainderman or reversioner; and in subsection (3), “leasehold
-- src:290 | tenant” includes a tenant for a term, a tenant under a periodical
-- src:291 | tenancy and a tenant at will.
@ref s 4(4) "leasehold tenant" (src:289-291)
GIVEN `the kind of tenancy` IS A `Kind of leasehold tenancy`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(4) the tenant is a leasehold tenant` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of tenancy`
    WHEN `Tenancy for a term` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Periodical tenancy` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Tenancy at will` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“leasehold tenant” includes a tenant for a term, a tenant under a periodical tenancy and a tenant at will"

-- src:295 | (5) An estate for life without impeachment of waste shall not
-- src:296 | confer, or be deemed to have conferred, upon the tenant for life any
-- src:297 | legal right to commit waste of the description known as equitable
-- src:298 | waste, unless an intention to confer such right expressly appears by
-- src:299 | the instrument creating such estate.
@ref s 4(5) (src:295-299)
GIVEN `the estate is an estate for life without impeachment of waste` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an intention to confer the right expressly appears by the instrument creating the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(5) the estate confers on the tenant for life a legal right to commit equitable waste` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the estate is an estate for life without impeachment of waste` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An estate for life without impeachment of waste"
        IF `an intention to confer the right expressly appears by the instrument creating the estate` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless an intention to confer such right expressly appears by the instrument creating such estate" -- a lifted bar grants nothing (fork QA)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not confer, or be deemed to have conferred, upon the tenant for life any legal right to commit waste of the description known as equitable waste"

-- src:303 | (6) There shall not be any merger by operation of law only of any
-- src:304 | estate the beneficial interest in which would not before 23 July 1909
-- src:305 | have been deemed to be merged or extinguished in equity.
@ref s 4(6) (src:303-305)
GIVEN `the estate would merge by operation of law only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the beneficial interest in the estate would not before 23 July 1909 have been deemed to be merged or extinguished in equity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(6) there is a merger by operation of law only of the estate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the estate would merge by operation of law only` AND `the beneficial interest in the estate would not before 23 July 1909 have been deemed to be merged or extinguished in equity` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "There shall not be any merger by operation of law only of any estate the beneficial interest in which would not before 23 July 1909 have been deemed to be merged or extinguished in equity"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any estate the beneficial interest in which would not before 23 July 1909 have been deemed to be merged"

§ `Section 4(7) -- mortgagors`

-- src:309 | (7) A mortgagor entitled for the time being to the possession or
-- src:310 | receipt of the rents and profits of any immovable property, as to which
-- src:311 | no notice of his intention to take possession, or to enter into the
-- src:312 | receipt of the rents and profits thereof, has been given by the
-- src:313 | mortgagee, may sue for such possession or for the recovery of such
-- src:314 | rents or profits or to prevent or recover damages in respect of any
-- src:315 | trespass or other wrong relative thereto in his own name only, unless
-- src:316 | the cause of action arises upon a lease or other contract made by him
-- src:317 | jointly with any other person.
@ref s 4(7) (src:309-317)
GIVEN `the mortgagor is entitled for the time being to the possession or receipt of the rents and profits of the immovable property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the mortgagee has given notice of his intention to take possession or to enter into the receipt of the rents and profits` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cause of action arises upon a lease or other contract made by the mortgagor jointly with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(7) the mortgagor may sue in his own name only` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the mortgagor is entitled for the time being to the possession or receipt of the rents and profits of the immovable property` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A mortgagor entitled for the time being to the possession or receipt of the rents and profits"
        IF `the mortgagee has given notice of his intention to take possession or to enter into the receipt of the rents and profits` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as to which no notice of his intention to take possession ... has been given by the mortgagee"
        IF `the cause of action arises upon a lease or other contract made by the mortgagor jointly with any other person` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the cause of action arises upon a lease or other contract made by him jointly with any other person" -- fork QA: a permission, not a bar, lifted by "unless" (the other reading is NOTHING, as for a lifted bar)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 4(8) -- assignment of debts and choses in action`

-- src:325 | (8) Any absolute assignment by writing under the hand of the
-- src:326 | assignor, not purporting to be by way of charge only, of any debt or
-- src:327 | other legal chose in action of which express notice in writing has been
-- src:328 | given to the debtor, trustee or other person from whom the assignor
-- src:329 | would have been entitled to receive or claim such debt or chose in
-- src:330 | action, shall be and be deemed to have been effectual in law, subject
-- src:331 | to all equities which would have been entitled to priority over the
-- src:332 | right of the assignee under the law as it existed before 23 July 1909, to
-- src:333 | pass and transfer the legal right to such debt or chose in action, from
-- src:334 | the date of such notice, and all legal and other remedies for the same,
-- src:335 | and the power to give a good discharge for the same, without the
-- src:336 | concurrence of the assignor.
@ref s 4(8) (src:325-336)
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the assignment is absolute` AND `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` AND (NOT `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only`) AND `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any absolute assignment by writing under the hand of the assignor, not purporting to be by way of charge only, ... of which express notice in writing has been given"

-- src:325 | (8) Any absolute assignment by writing under the hand of the
-- src:326 | assignor, not purporting to be by way of charge only, of any debt or
-- src:327 | other legal chose in action of which express notice in writing has been
-- src:328 | given to the debtor, trustee or other person from whom the assignor
-- src:329 | would have been entitled to receive or claim such debt or chose in
-- src:330 | action, shall be and be deemed to have been effectual in law, subject
-- src:331 | to all equities which would have been entitled to priority over the
-- src:332 | right of the assignee under the law as it existed before 23 July 1909, to
-- src:333 | pass and transfer the legal right to such debt or chose in action, from
-- src:334 | the date of such notice, and all legal and other remedies for the same,
-- src:335 | and the power to give a good discharge for the same, without the
-- src:336 | concurrence of the assignor.
@ref s 4(8) the date from which the legal right passes (src:325-336)
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which express notice in writing was given to the debtor` IS A DATE
      `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 4(8) the date from which the legal right to the debt or chose in action passes` MEANS
    IF `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` `the assignment is absolute` `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST `the date on which express notice in writing was given to the debtor` -- "from the date of such notice"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the date is given only for an assignment within the subsection

-- src:333 | pass and transfer the legal right to such debt or chose in action, from
-- src:334 | the date of such notice, and all legal and other remedies for the same,
@ref s 4(8) whether the legal right has passed on the day asked about (src:333-334)
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which express notice in writing was given to the debtor` IS A DATE
      `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) the legal right to the debt or chose in action has passed by the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 4(8) the date from which the legal right to the debt or chose in action passes` `the assignment is absolute` `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` `the date on which express notice in writing was given to the debtor` `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right passes only under an assignment within the subsection
    WHEN JUST passes THEN
        IF `the day asked about` AT LEAST passes
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "from the date of such notice"
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to pass and transfer the legal right to such debt or chose in action, from the date of such notice" -- the right passes under this subsection from the date of the notice, so on an earlier day it has not passed under it; this is an effect that starts on a date, not a scope statement about which assignments the subsection reaches, so it is not a site of fork F-DATE-GATE

-- src:335 | and the power to give a good discharge for the same, without the
-- src:336 | concurrence of the assignor.
@ref s 4(8) the power to give a good discharge (src:335-336)
GIVEN `the assignment is absolute` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) the assignee has the power to give a good discharge for the debt or chose in action without the concurrence of the assignor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` `the assignment is absolute` `the assignment is by writing under the hand of the assignor` `the assignment purports to be by way of charge only` `express notice in writing has been given to the debtor trustee or other person from whom the assignor would have been entitled to receive or claim the debt or chose in action` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE -- "and the power to give a good discharge for the same, without the concurrence of the assignor"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power passes only under an assignment within the subsection

-- src:330 | action, shall be and be deemed to have been effectual in law, subject
-- src:331 | to all equities which would have been entitled to priority over the
-- src:332 | right of the assignee under the law as it existed before 23 July 1909, to
-- src:333 | pass and transfer the legal right to such debt or chose in action, from
@ref s 4(8) subject to equities (src:330-333)
GIVEN `the equity would have been entitled to priority over the right of the assignee under the law as it existed before 23 July 1909` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(8) the assignee takes subject to the equity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the equity would have been entitled to priority over the right of the assignee under the law as it existed before 23 July 1909` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "subject to all equities which would have been entitled to priority over the right of the assignee under the law as it existed before 23 July 1909"

§ `Section 4(9) to (13) -- stipulations, injunctions, interim relief, equity to prevail`

-- src:341 | (9) Stipulations in contracts, as to time or otherwise, which would
-- src:342 | not, before 23 July 1909, have been deemed to be or to have become
-- src:343 | of the essence of such contracts in a court of equity, shall receive in all
-- src:344 | cases the same construction and effect as they would have received in
-- src:345 | equity before that date.
@ref s 4(9) (src:341-345)
GIVEN `before 23 July 1909 a court of equity would not have deemed the stipulation as to time or otherwise to be or to have become of the essence of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(9) the stipulation is construed and has effect as it would have had in equity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `before 23 July 1909 a court of equity would not have deemed the stipulation as to time or otherwise to be or to have become of the essence of the contract` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Stipulations in contracts, as to time or otherwise, which would not, before 23 July 1909, have been deemed to be or to have become of the essence"

-- src:350 | (10) A Mandatory Order or an injunction may be granted or a
-- src:351 | receiver appointed by an interlocutory order of the court, either
-- src:352 | unconditionally or upon such terms and conditions as the court thinks
-- src:353 | just, in all cases in which it appears to the court to be just or
-- src:354 | convenient that such order should be made.
@ref s 4(10) (src:350-354)
GIVEN `it appears to the court to be just or convenient that the order should be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(10) the court may grant a Mandatory Order or an injunction or appoint a receiver by an interlocutory order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it appears to the court to be just or convenient that the order should be made` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in all cases in which it appears to the court to be just or convenient" -- the words say the order may be made in all such cases, not that it may be made only in them (fork F-W3)

-- src:360 | (10A) Subject to subsections (10B), (10C) and (10D), a court has
-- src:361 | the power to grant interim relief in aid of proceedings in any civil or
-- src:362 | commercial matter (excluding proceedings arising out of any fiscal,
-- src:363 | monetary or revenue law or measure) which have been or are to be
