-- src:369 | convenient that such order should be made.
@ref s 4(10A) (src:360-369)
GIVEN `the proceedings are in a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings arise out of a fiscal monetary or revenue law or measure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings have been or are to be commenced outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the court to be just or convenient that the order should be made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(10A) the court has the power to grant interim relief in aid of the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are in a civil or commercial matter` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings in any civil or commercial matter"
        IF `the proceedings arise out of a fiscal monetary or revenue law or measure` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(excluding proceedings arising out of any fiscal, monetary or revenue law or measure)" -- fork QE: a bracket narrowing what a grant of power reaches, with no "only" and no "means"; s 4(10D) below is a "means" definition and answers JUST FALSE; the other reading is JUST FALSE here too
        IF NOT `the proceedings have been or are to be commenced outside Singapore` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which have been or are to be commenced outside Singapore"
        IF `it appears to the court to be just or convenient that the order should be made` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it appears to the court to be just or convenient that such order should be made" -- MARGINAL (a)

