        IF `the proceedings concerned are not capable of giving rise to a judgment which may be enforced in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court may refuse to make an order under subsection (10A) if —" -- MARGINAL (a)

-- src:392 | (10D) In subsection (10A), “interim relief”, in relation to the court
-- src:393 | before which an application is brought, means interim relief of any
-- src:394 | kind which that court has power to grant in proceedings relating to
-- src:395 | matters within its jurisdiction, other than —
-- src:397 | (a) a warrant for the arrest of property; or
-- src:399 | (b) provision for obtaining evidence.
@ref s 4(10D) (src:392-399)
GIVEN `the relief is interim relief of a kind which the court has power to grant in proceedings relating to matters within its jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relief is a warrant for the arrest of property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relief is provision for obtaining evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(10D) the relief is interim relief` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the relief is a warrant for the arrest of property` OR `the relief is provision for obtaining evidence` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than — (a) a warrant for the arrest of property; or (b) provision for obtaining evidence" -- a "means" definition (fork QE)
        IF `the relief is interim relief of a kind which the court has power to grant in proceedings relating to matters within its jurisdiction` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“interim relief” ... means interim relief of any kind which that court has power to grant"

-- src:405 | (11) If an injunction is asked, either before, or at, or after the
-- src:406 | hearing of any cause or matter, to prevent any threatened or
-- src:407 | apprehended waste or trespass, the injunction may be granted if the
-- src:408 | court thinks fit whether the person against whom the injunction is
-- src:409 | sought is or is not in possession under any claim of title or otherwise,
-- src:410 | or, if out of possession, does or does not claim, a right to do the act
-- src:411 | sought to be restrained under any colour of title, and whether the
-- src:412 | estates claimed by both, or by either of the parties, are legal or
-- src:413 | equitable.
@ref s 4(11) (src:405-413)
GIVEN `an injunction is asked to prevent a threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(11) the injunction may be granted to prevent the threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an injunction is asked to prevent a threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an injunction is asked, either before, or at, or after the hearing of any cause or matter, to prevent any threatened or apprehended waste or trespass" -- MARGINAL (b) F-W2: the opening "If an injunction is asked ..." is read as the subject of the rule, not as a condition whose failure is the text's no
        IF `the court thinks fit` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the injunction may be granted if the court thinks fit" -- MARGINAL (a)

-- src:408 | court thinks fit whether the person against whom the injunction is
-- src:409 | sought is or is not in possession under any claim of title or otherwise,
-- src:410 | or, if out of possession, does or does not claim, a right to do the act
-- src:411 | sought to be restrained under any colour of title, and whether the
-- src:412 | estates claimed by both, or by either of the parties, are legal or
-- src:413 | equitable.
@ref s 4(11) possession and title are immaterial (src:408-413)
GIVEN `an injunction is asked to prevent a threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(11) it matters whether the person is in possession or claims a right under colour of title or whether the estates are legal or equitable` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an injunction is asked to prevent a threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "whether the person against whom the injunction is sought is or is not in possession under any claim of title or otherwise, ... and whether the estates claimed by both, or by either of the parties, are legal or equitable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If an injunction is asked ... to prevent any threatened or apprehended waste or trespass"

-- src:420 | (12) In questions relating to the custody and education of minors,
-- src:421 | the rules of equity shall prevail.
@ref s 4(12) (src:420-421)
GIVEN `the question relates to the custody and education of minors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(12) the rules of equity prevail` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the question relates to the custody and education of minors` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In questions relating to the custody and education of minors"

-- src:427 | (13) Generally in all matters not particularly mentioned in this
-- src:428 | section, in which there is any conflict or variance between the rules of
-- src:429 | equity and the rules of the common law with reference to the same
-- src:430 | matter, the rules of equity shall prevail.
@ref s 4(13) (src:427-430)
GIVEN `the matter is not particularly mentioned in section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a conflict or variance between the rules of equity and the rules of the common law with reference to the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 4(13) the rules of equity prevail over the rules of the common law` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter is not particularly mentioned in section 4` AND `there is a conflict or variance between the rules of equity and the rules of the common law with reference to the same matter` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Generally in all matters not particularly mentioned in this section, in which there is any conflict or variance"

§§ `Section 4 -- tests`

-- Fixtures: the three kinds of administration and the facts of an ordinary case.
`s 4(1) a deceased estate` MEANS `Administration by a court of a deceased person's estate that proves insufficient to pay debts and liabilities in full`
`s 4(1) a company winding up` MEANS `Winding up of a company under the Insolvency Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018 whose assets prove insufficient`

#ASSERT `s 4(1) the rules in force under the law of bankruptcy prevail and are to be observed` `s 4(1) a deceased estate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "the same rules shall prevail"
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the rules in force under the law of bankruptcy prevail and are to be observed` `s 4(1) a company winding up` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- a company winding up
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the rules in force under the law of bankruptcy prevail and are to be observed` `s 4(1) a deceased estate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a question the subsection does not name
#ASSERT `s 4(1) the rules in force under the law of bankruptcy prevail and are to be observed` `Another kind of administration` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- another administration
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the person may come in under the decree or order and make claims against the estate or the company` `s 4(1) a deceased estate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may come in under the decree or order"
#ASSERT `s 4(2) the person may come in under the decree or order and make claims against the estate or the company` `s 4(1) a company winding up` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not entitled to prove
-- s 4(3): tenant for life or lives, or leasehold tenant
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the tenant may commit voluntary waste` `Tenant for life or lives` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not commit voluntary waste"
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the tenant may commit voluntary waste` `Leasehold tenant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a leasehold tenant
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the tenant may commit voluntary waste` `Leasehold tenant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an estate or tenancy without impeachment of waste: the bar is lifted and grants nothing
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the tenant may commit voluntary waste` `Leasehold tenant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a licence to commit waste
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the tenant may commit voluntary waste` `Another kind of occupier` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a tenant for life or lives or a leasehold tenant
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the prohibition of voluntary waste applies to the tenant` `Tenant for life or lives` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the prohibition applies
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the prohibition of voluntary waste applies to the tenant` `Tenant for life or lives` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not apply to any estate or tenancy without impeachment of waste"
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the prohibition of voluntary waste applies to the tenant` `Tenant for life or lives` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "or affect any licence or other right to commit waste"
#ASSERT `s 4(3) the prohibition of voluntary waste applies to the tenant` `Another kind of occupier` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not within the subsection
-- The regulative rule, run: a breach when waste is committed, a standing prohibition when nothing happens.
-- (#TRACE prints FULFILLED / a residual / BREACH and no assertion line; read below.)
-- With the prohibition applying and waste committed at day 5: DEONTIC BREACHED, BY the tenant.
#TRACE `s 4(3) the tenant shall not commit voluntary waste` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tenant for life or leasehold tenant` DOES `commit voluntary waste` AT 5
-- With the prohibition applying and nothing done: the prohibition stands (MUST NOT ... residual).
#TRACE `s 4(3) the tenant shall not commit voluntary waste` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 10
-- Without the prohibition (an estate without impeachment of waste): FULFILLED even if waste is committed.
#TRACE `s 4(3) the tenant shall not commit voluntary waste` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The tenant for life or leasehold tenant` DOES `commit voluntary waste` AT 5
-- s 4(4)
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the tenant is liable in damages to the remainderman or reversioner` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall be liable in damages"
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the tenant is liable in damages to the remainderman or reversioner` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no infringement of (3)
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the tenant is a leasehold tenant` `Tenancy for a term` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "a tenant for a term"
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the tenant is a leasehold tenant` `Periodical tenancy` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "a tenant under a periodical tenancy"
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the tenant is a leasehold tenant` `Tenancy at will` EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "a tenant at will"
#ASSERT `s 4(4) the tenant is a leasehold tenant` `Another kind of tenancy` EQUALS NOTHING -- "includes" does not close the list
-- s 4(5)
#ASSERT `s 4(5) the estate confers on the tenant for life a legal right to commit equitable waste` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "shall not confer ... any legal right to commit waste of the description known as equitable waste"
#ASSERT `s 4(5) the estate confers on the tenant for life a legal right to commit equitable waste` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- an intention expressly appears: "unless"
#ASSERT `s 4(5) the estate confers on the tenant for life a legal right to commit equitable waste` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an estate for life without impeachment of waste
-- s 4(6)
#ASSERT `s 4(6) there is a merger by operation of law only of the estate` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "There shall not be any merger by operation of law only"
#ASSERT `s 4(6) there is a merger by operation of law only of the estate` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a merger that equity would have recognised before 23 July 1909
#ASSERT `s 4(6) there is a merger by operation of law only of the estate` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a merger by operation of law only
-- s 4(7)
#ASSERT `s 4(7) the mortgagor may sue in his own name only` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may sue for such possession ... in his own name only"
#ASSERT `s 4(7) the mortgagor may sue in his own name only` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- the mortgagee has given notice
#ASSERT `s 4(7) the mortgagor may sue in his own name only` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a lease or contract made jointly with another person: "unless"
#ASSERT `s 4(7) the mortgagor may sue in his own name only` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not entitled to possession or the rents and profits
-- s 4(8)
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all four conditions met
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no express notice in writing given to the debtor
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- purports to be by way of charge only
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not absolute
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignment is effectual in law to pass the legal right to the debt or chose in action` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not in writing under the hand of the assignor
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the date from which the legal right to the debt or chose in action passes` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 14 3 2025) -- "from the date of such notice"
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the date from which the legal right to the debt or chose in action passes` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no notice, so no date
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the legal right to the debt or chose in action has passed by the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE (Date 13 3 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the day before the notice: the right passes from the date of the notice
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the legal right to the debt or chose in action has passed by the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day of the notice: "from the date of such notice"
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the legal right to the debt or chose in action has passed by the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE -- the day after the notice
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the legal right to the debt or chose in action has passed by the day` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 14 3 2025) FALSE (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- no express notice in writing given, so the subsection is not reached
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the legal right to the debt or chose in action has passed by the day` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 14 3 2025) TRUE (Date 15 3 2025) EQUALS NOTHING -- an assignment by way of charge only is outside the subsection
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignee has the power to give a good discharge for the debt or chose in action without the concurrence of the assignor` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- all four conditions met
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignee has the power to give a good discharge for the debt or chose in action without the concurrence of the assignor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no express notice in writing given
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignee has the power to give a good discharge for the debt or chose in action without the concurrence of the assignor` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- by way of charge only
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignee takes subject to the equity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "subject to all equities which would have been entitled to priority"
#ASSERT `s 4(8) the assignee takes subject to the equity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an equity that would not have had priority
-- s 4(9)
#ASSERT `s 4(9) the stipulation is construed and has effect as it would have had in equity` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "shall receive in all cases the same construction and effect"
#ASSERT `s 4(9) the stipulation is construed and has effect as it would have had in equity` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- a stipulation equity would have treated as of the essence
-- s 4(10)
#ASSERT `s 4(10) the court may grant a Mandatory Order or an injunction or appoint a receiver by an interlocutory order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- just or convenient
#ASSERT `s 4(10) the court may grant a Mandatory Order or an injunction or appoint a receiver by an interlocutory order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- "in all cases in which" does not say "only"
-- s 4(10A) to (10D)
#ASSERT `s 4(10A) the court has the power to grant interim relief in aid of the proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- civil matter, outside Singapore, just or convenient
#ASSERT `s 4(10A) the court has the power to grant interim relief in aid of the proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- not just or convenient: "if it appears to the court to be just or convenient"
#ASSERT `s 4(10A) the court has the power to grant interim relief in aid of the proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a fiscal, monetary or revenue matter: "excluding"
#ASSERT `s 4(10A) the court has the power to grant interim relief in aid of the proceedings` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- not a civil or commercial matter
#ASSERT `s 4(10A) the court has the power to grant interim relief in aid of the proceedings` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- proceedings in Singapore only
#ASSERT `s 4(10B) the order may be made either unconditionally or upon terms and conditions the court thinks just` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "either unconditionally or upon such terms"
#ASSERT `s 4(10B) the order may be made either unconditionally or upon terms and conditions the court thinks just` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not an order under (10A)
#ASSERT `s 4(10C) the court may refuse to make an order under subsection (10A)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (a) inappropriate for want of other jurisdiction
#ASSERT `s 4(10C) the court may refuse to make an order under subsection (10A)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- (b) no enforceable judgment
#ASSERT `s 4(10C) the court may refuse to make an order under subsection (10A)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- neither (a) nor (b): "if"
#ASSERT `s 4(10D) the relief is interim relief` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- interim relief of a kind the court can grant
#ASSERT `s 4(10D) the relief is interim relief` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- a warrant for the arrest of property: "other than"
#ASSERT `s 4(10D) the relief is interim relief` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- provision for obtaining evidence: "other than"
#ASSERT `s 4(10D) the relief is interim relief` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- relief the court has no power to grant: "means"
-- s 4(11) to (13)
#ASSERT `s 4(11) the injunction may be granted to prevent the threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "may be granted if the court thinks fit"
#ASSERT `s 4(11) the injunction may be granted to prevent the threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- the court does not think fit
#ASSERT `s 4(11) the injunction may be granted to prevent the threatened or apprehended waste or trespass` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- an injunction not asked to prevent waste or trespass
#ASSERT `s 4(11) it matters whether the person is in possession or claims a right under colour of title or whether the estates are legal or equitable` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE -- "whether ... is or is not in possession"
#ASSERT `s 4(11) it matters whether the person is in possession or claims a right under colour of title or whether the estates are legal or equitable` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- an injunction for another purpose
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the rules of equity prevail` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- "the rules of equity shall prevail"
#ASSERT `s 4(12) the rules of equity prevail` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- not custody and education of minors
#ASSERT `s 4(13) the rules of equity prevail over the rules of the common law` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE -- an unmentioned matter in conflict
#ASSERT `s 4(13) the rules of equity prevail over the rules of the common law` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING -- a matter particularly mentioned in section 4
#ASSERT `s 4(13) the rules of equity prevail over the rules of the common law` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING -- no conflict or variance
